Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 04:35:00 +0000
Subject: csm-xsmp-client.c: Clear the watch id when the IO watch stops

When client_iochannel_watch() returns FALSE, GLib destroys the source,
but watch_id kept its id, and csm_xsmp_client_disconnect() would remove
it again at finalize. Clear it before the client's reference is dropped,
since that can finalize the client.

Assisted-by: Claude Code:claude-opus-5
---
--- a/cinnamon-session/csm-xsmp-client.c
+++ b/cinnamon-session/csm-xsmp-client.c
@@ -107,6 +107,9 @@ client_iochannel_watch (GIOChannel    *c
         default:
                 g_assert_not_reached ();
         }
+        if (! keep_going) {
+                client->priv->watch_id = 0;
+        }
         g_object_unref (client);
 
         return keep_going;
